    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (there is one test file, `AcceptanceTest`, and it is green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required an owner's `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived DTO fields (like `membershipLevel` \u2192 `MembershipLevelCalculator`, `identityKey` \u2192 `IdentityKey`):\n\n1. **`util/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility utility with a static `of(String)` that computes the standard Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in a string, ignoring non-digit characters (so `\"SMI-0007\"` is checked over `\"0007\"`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` field to the `Owner` schema (`integer`, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed right after `customerCode`. The DTO is generated from this spec.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)` and a small `computeCheckDigit(owner)` default method that delegates to `LuhnCheckDigit`, returning `null` when the customer code is absent (mirroring how `formatMembershipNumber` handles a missing code).\n\nNo logic was duplicated \u2014 the mapper just delegates \u2014 and the Luhn algorithm lives in its own reusable unit alongside the other derivation helpers.",
